Feature: Native Gmail message resources and uploads
  Scenario: Gmail body corrections preserve source contracts
    Then six Gmail body corrections retain shared schemas authentication and reversible media declarations

  Scenario: Gmail source drift cannot be partially corrected
    Then changed Gmail identities resources and upload contracts reject before correction

  Scenario: Both importers expose Gmail JSON and MIME inputs
    Then six Gmail operations expose qualified resource and MIME fields without changing canonical paths

  Scenario: Native Gmail requests preserve all supported body modes
    Then native Gmail private requests retain JSON simple MIME and metadata with MIME wire contracts

  Scenario: Gmail related bodies retain exact bytes and boundaries
    Then Gmail related uploads retain UTF8 metadata and exact bounded message bytes

  Scenario: Invalid Gmail uploads cannot dispatch
    Then malformed Gmail files resources and upload overrides fail before private HTTP

  Scenario: Gmail body choices are included in private authority
    Then changed Gmail paths body profiles and MIME limits cannot reuse approved credentials

  Scenario: Saved Gmail connections keep metadata variables private
    Then a saved Gmail connection resolves private draft metadata inside a related upload

  Scenario: Anonymous Gmail related transport owns its boundary header
    Then the anonymous HTTP executor preserves the related upload boundary and both parts
